    {
      "id": "summary-exploit-plan-1780566355",
      "summary_id": "summary-exploit-plan-1780566355",
      "source_plan_id": "plan-1780566355",
      "phase": "exploit",
      "completed_tasks": "[\"Enumerate SMB users via RID cycling null session on port 10139. Use netexec_smb_users to brute-force RIDs and discover all domain user accounts without authentication.\", \"Enumerate SMB shares via null session on port 10139. Use netexec_smb_shares to list all accessible shares and their permissions. Also use smbmap_enum for comprehensive share enumeration including readable shares and their contents.\", \"Perform comprehensive SMB enumeration using smbmap_enum on port 10139 with null session. This checks share listing, directory contents, and file read permissions in a single tool call \\u2014 may reveal flag files directly.\", \"Perform AS-REP roasting against Kerberos on port 10088. Use impacket_GetNPUsers with the user list compiled from LDAP and SMB enumeration. If previous tasks yielded no user list, use a minimal list containing common AD accounts: Administrator, Guest, krbtgt, user, admin, defaultaccount.\", \"Retry LDAP anonymous enumeration using raw ldapsearch via shell_exec. First discover the base DN, then dump all objects and grep for flag patterns and user SAM account names. Save usernames to /tmp/users.txt for AS-REP roasting.\", \"Perform AS-REP roasting against Kerberos on port 10088 using the user list from LDAP enumeration. Include domain parameter. If /tmp/users.txt is empty or missing from LDAP, fall back to common AD accounts.\", \"Enumerate MSRPC service on port 10135 using rpcclient with null session. Discover domain users, groups, and accessible pipes. Save any discovered usernames to /tmp/users.txt if LDAP enumeration yielded nothing.\", \"Perform anonymous LDAP enumeration on port 10389 via shell_exec. Discover base DN, dump all objects (users, groups, computers), extract sAMAccountNames to /tmp/users.txt, and grep for flag patterns in all LDAP attributes (description, info, comment, division, streetAddress, wWWHomePage).\", \"Enumerate MSRPC service on port 10135 using rpcclient with null session. Discover domain users and save to /tmp/users.txt if LDAP fails. Also query domain SID via lsaquery.\"]",
      "key_findings": "{\"flags_found\": [], \"endpoints\": 0}",
      "failed_approaches": "[\"Perform anonymous LDAP bind enumeration on port 10389 to discover domain users, groups, computers, and search for flag-related attributes. Use ldapsearch_ad to dump all user objects and check description/info fields for flag patterns.\", \"If HTTP service on port 10080 returned a web application, perform directory brute-force enumeration using dirb_scan to discover hidden endpoints, admin panels, API paths, or file upload endpoints that may contain or lead to flag files.\", \"Directly search LDAP for flag values in common AD attributes. Use ldapsearch_ad with a broad filter to retrieve all user/computer/group objects and grep for 'flag' pattern in all returned attributes (description, info, comment, displayName, department, title, streetAddress, physicalDeliveryOfficeName).\", \"Probe HTTP service on port 10080. Use curl_get to retrieve the root page and check for web applications, APIs, or flag files served over HTTP.\"]",
      "created_at": "2026-06-04T18:02:22",
      "type": "PlanSummary",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-04T18:02:22.710705",
      "_version": 1
    }
